# Wealth inequality for white males vs white females, NLSY-79-based sample (1990 vs 1996)

**Population:** race == 'white', full sample (n = 7,099; male 3,469, female 3,630). Wealth = supplied composite wealth variables (sums of five NLS wealth items); unweighted sample descriptives only. Primary analysis on full white sample; ever_jailed = 0 rerun as sensitivity. Negatives floored to 0 (bottom-coded) for Gini and top-decile shares; percentile ratios only where the denominator percentile > 0. P90/P10 and P75/P25 are NOT computable because P10 = 0 and P25 = 0 for every sex-year cell; replaced with P90/P50, P75/P50, P95/P50.

